WEBVTT

cd-en-001
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.323
At noon, witnesses reported a bell
sounding from a tower that has no bell.

cd-en-002
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:11.876
The tower's mounting frame was empty, and no
instrument capable of making that sound was found.

cd-en-003
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:19.225
The reported sound and empty frame are established, but
no bell or sound-making mechanism has been confirmed.

cd-en-004
00:00:20.182 --> 00:00:23.500
The source of that reported
sound remains unidentified.

cd-en-005
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.750
Clock repairer Mira is examining clues
connected to her missing brother.

cd-en-006
00:00:32.764 --> 00:00:36.342
A note said to be his was left
among the workshop materials.

cd-en-007
00:00:40.356 --> 00:00:45.283
A brass moth appears beside the note, but
its meaning and purpose remain unknown.

cd-en-008
00:00:49.297 --> 00:00:55.245
Clocks and records repeat the time nine seventeen,
linking the note, moth, and recorded time.

cd-en-009
00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:04.499
Together, those items form a clue chain,
not proof of her brother's location.

cd-en-010
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:09.851
The note directs the investigation
toward a ledger arranged in two columns.

cd-en-011
00:01:13.737 --> 00:01:17.963
One column records minutes, while
the other records people's names.

cd-en-012
00:01:21.849 --> 00:01:27.286
The visible pages establish those two
categories, but no causal action by the ledger.

cd-en-013
00:01:31.172 --> 00:01:36.500
They do not prove that the ledger steals time,
removes people, or records genuine losses.

cd-en-014
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:41.690
The missing brother's note points the
investigation toward the city council.

cd-en-015
00:01:45.597 --> 00:01:50.486
That note records an allegation, not evidence
confirming the council's involvement.

cd-en-016
00:01:54.393 --> 00:01:58.131
The ledger's origin and
authenticity also remain unverified.

cd-en-017
00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:06.499
No available material establishes the
council's responsibility or motive.

cd-en-018
00:02:10.406 --> 00:02:15.500
No known mechanism connects the council,
ledger, missing brother, and tower incident.

cd-en-019
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:25.125
Confirmed items include the reported bell, empty frame,
note, brass moth, nine seventeen, and two-column ledger.

cd-en-020
00:02:27.765 --> 00:02:31.434
The ledger records minutes and
names as two separate categories.

cd-en-021
00:02:34.074 --> 00:02:38.510
Those categories are described without
claiming that either records a real loss.

cd-en-022
00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:45.046
The sound's source and the missing
brother's location remain unconfirmed.

cd-en-023
00:02:47.686 --> 00:02:51.907
Any connection between the evidence and
the council also remains unconfirmed.

cd-en-024
00:02:54.547 --> 00:02:59.500
With those evidential limits unchanged,
the tower remains under investigation.
